===== event-trigger (SKIPPED) =====
SKIPPED
reason: flow 6 produced no object number, so there is nothing this run caused whose indexing could be observed; a broker transit cannot be asserted from an ambient query
trigger-action: create the object whose write publishes the event, performed by flow 6
trigger-endpoint: http://localhost:20050/arkcase/api/latest/plugin/complaint
trigger-response-body: (not observed — the trigger action did not execute)
note: the trigger half is not the evidence for this flow.  A capture showing
  only an accepted request proves nothing about the criterion, which is that
  the message is DELIVERED with an identical payload.  It is recorded anyway
  so that the pair stays complete and the halves keep their order.

===== event-delivery (SKIPPED) =====
SKIPPED
reason: flow 6 produced no object number, so there is nothing this run caused whose indexing could be observed; a broker transit cannot be asserted from an ambient query
destination-name: (not observed — no event was produced this run)
message-payload-as-delivered: (not observed — no event was produced this run)
declared-type-or-format: (not observed — no event was produced this run)
message-priority: (not observed — no event was produced this run)
message-persistence: (not observed — no event was produced this run)
application-set-properties: (not observed — no event was produced this run)
observation-mode: indirect
observation-means: delivery is observed through its downstream effect — the
  object this run created becoming findable through the application search
  endpoint recorded below, which requires that an event this run produced
  was published to the broker and consumed by the indexing pipeline.
  Nothing here reads a message off a destination: no broker client library
  is used, and the tooling is a shell with the transport client, the text
  utilities and the date utility, nothing more.
observation-endpoint: http://localhost:20050/arkcase/api/latest/plugin/search/advancedSearch
polling-window-configured: 12 attempts at 5s
replay-requirement: the replay must observe delivery by the SAME indirect
  means, through the same endpoint and within the same polling window.  An
  indirect observation compared against a differently obtained one is not a
  comparison, and an unstated one is not evidence at all.
messaging-api-occurrences-measured-at-run-time: 46
messaging-api-census-command: find <repo> <prune build output, installed
  dependencies, object storage and scratch trees> -name '*.java' -exec grep -h
  javax.jms {} + | wc -l
messaging-api-resolution: every occurrence resolves from the broker client
  library rather than from the platform runtime, so the removal of the
  platform enterprise modules required no reinstatement at all for
  messaging.  The client version is consequently HELD on purpose: a version
  change without a demonstrated incompatibility would be a change without a
  reason, and a change to a client that speaks a wire protocol is a
  wire-behaviour risk by definition.
residual-risk-classification: the integration framework that routes some
  events is residual risk with WEAK concern.  The workflow engine that flow
  7 exercises is SUBSTANTIVE residual risk.  The two are deliberately kept
  apart, because merging them would either overstate this flow or
  understate that one.
volatile-values-normalised-when-present: the broker-assigned message
  identifier; a correlation identifier where the broker GENERATED it, never
  where the application set it; the enqueue and expiry instants; the
  redelivery counter; the connection and client identifier; and the generic
  set — other instants, session identifiers, generated request identifiers,
  the response header that sets a cookie, the response header carrying
  wall-clock time, entity validators and absolute filesystem paths.
behaviour-bearing-values-preserved-verbatim: the destination name; the
  payload content; the declared type; the priority and persistence flags;
  and every application-set property on the message.  Not one of them is
  normalised, and not one of them is invented to fill a field: each is
  recorded above as not observed, because no message was delivered.
broker-data-directory-created-or-referenced: none.  The conventional name
  for a broker data directory is a bare pattern in the repository ignore
  file, matched at any depth, so a file written under it would be silently
  uncommitted while every local check still passed.  It is neither created
  nor spelled here; only the three capture files of this flow are written.
governing-rules-provenance: the project rules facility reports, verbatim,
  "No user rules provided", and there is no on-disk rules document.  The
  rules that govern this work are nonetheless present and binding: an
  embedded, numbered block of seven, governing in full exactly as an
  external rules document would.  The identifiers used to cite them are a
  convention of this migration rather than quoted titles, and nothing is
  invented and nothing is softened.
baseline-comparison-requirement: this capture and the JDK 8 baseline capture
  of the same flow must differ in nothing but values this script
  normalises.  An absence recorded as an absence is comparable; the same
  absence filled in would not be.

